      "urpx:forRatePlan": {
        "@id": "gpc:rlg"
      },
      "urpx:hasCoverageClaim": {
        "@id": "gpc:cc-rlg-2026-06-01",
        "@type": "urpx:CoverageClaim",
        "urpx:completenessResult": {
          "@id": "urpx:partial"
        },
        "urpx:selfContained": true,
        "urpx:explainedBy": {
          "@type": "urpx:Evaluation",
          "@id": "gpc:cc-rlg-2026-06-01-evaluation",
          "urpx:evaluationKind": {
            "@id": "urpx:coverageEvaluation"
          },
          "urpx:description": "This filing does not carry everything its source document states. 5 parts are deferred, listed here in the same words as the filing's tariff.toml [modeling].deferrals so the two records cannot drift. (1) Lights counts. Each light charge is priced per light of one kind. URPX v0.5.1 names no profile property for a count of lights of a kind, so each light's MetricInput is a urpx:profileMetricInput that names no urpx:profileMetricProperty and states the kind in its name, in the pattern of Jackson EMC's Schedule S-26; a consumer supplies the counts. (2) Municipal Franchise Fee base. MFF-11 applies to the total revenues of each bill, which include the ECCR-15 and DSM-C-15 amounts. Its multiplier Prices here are based on each light charge's Price, not on the ECCR and DSM-C multiplier Prices, so the franchise fee on those two amounts, about 0.44 percent of the base bill inside city limits, is not carried. (3) Energy and Fuel Cost Recovery. RLG-9's rates do not include energy; the customer contracts for it on EOL-19 or TOU-EOL-11, whose filings carry its price and fuel. The sheet's Fuel Cost Recovery section increases \"the amount calculated at the above rate\", but RLG-9 prices no kWh, so no fuel is carried here. (4) Pole and construction charges. The sheet prices standard poles from $418.16 to $1,936.93 as a non-refundable Contribution In Aid of Construction paid before construction; a customer may pay $50.00 for each luminaire removed when the Company replaces a Company-owned system, $2.49 per foot of excess underground trench over 80 feet per pole, a CIAC for taller poles or relocation, and a CIAC for spending above five times the estimated annual base revenue, and may reimburse maintenance from vandalism; tree trimming is the customer's. None is a monthly charge and none is carried. (5) Term of Contract. At least five years and thereafter until terminated on six months' written notice, with an advance payment of up to half the estimated annual revenue. Nothing is priced by it and it is not carried.",
          "urpx:evaluatedOn": "2026-10-19T00:00:00"
        }
      }
    }
  }
